Subject: sd_limits, sd_lim, sdqueuex: a disk controller's limits (C4-7)

Contract C4-7, kabi k30.1.6 / k46.1.7.  A controller that registered
(queuefn, c) with sd_register may attach a struct sdlim to that
registration from the same _load (sd_limits: EBUSY after sd's first
open, ENOENT for another module's or no registration, EINVAL for a
field out of range, each with one console line).  The limits sit in
dlm_sdlim[] beside dlm_sdreg[]; dlm_sdreg's layout, which sd reads, is
unchanged, and the backstop sweep removes both.  The core keeps no card
numbers: sd_lim(card) and sdqueuex(cpx) find a card's registration by
what the four-card sd's sdcardbase and sdhardwarename return (the
registration's base and name); two registrations alike get no limits.
sdqueuex gives the extended command to the card's sl_queue, and
completes it at once (okay 0, sx_resid nbyte) for a card with none.
include/sys/sdseg.h is the header the kit ships.  The state harness
covers each case.

